# Version on commit

`internal/version/version.go` holds the release identifier logged at startup.

When the user asks to create a git commit:

1. Ask which version to set for this commit. Do not guess or auto-increment.
2. After they answer, update `const Version` in `internal/version/version.go` to that value.
3. Include the version file in the same commit.
4. Do not commit if they have not given a version.

This commit ships `0.9.3`. Later commits need a new version from the user.
